<BaseLayout
  title="Buy Land in Texas"
  description="Buying a farm, ranch, or recreational property in Texas? Honest Acres Group evaluates water, soils, ag valuation, and wildlife like a working rancher — before you offer."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Buy land with somebody who works it</h1>
      <p>
        Buying rural land is not like buying a house. The value is in things
        that don't show up in pretty photos: reliable water, soil that grows
        grass, a valid ag valuation, fences that hold, access that holds up in
        wet weather, and wildlife habitat that's real — not promised.
      </p>

      <h2>What we check on every tract</h2>
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="card"><h3>Water</h3><p>Tanks, creeks, wells, and water rights — where it is, how reliable it is in a dry year, and what it would cost to add.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Soils &amp; production</h3><p>What the ground will grow and carry, from native pasture to improved Bermuda hay fields.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Ag valuation &amp; taxes</h3><p>Whether the property carries an agricultural valuation, what it takes to keep it, and what losing it would cost.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Wildlife &amp; recreation</h3><p>Habitat, food, cover, and pressure from neighbors — the things that decide whether a place hunts well.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Minerals &amp; rights</h3><p>What conveys, what doesn't, and what questions to ask before closing — with the right professionals brought in.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Access &amp; boundaries</h3><p>Legal access, easements, and fence lines checked against surveys, not assumptions.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>1. Tell us what you're after</strong> — acreage, county, budget, and what the land needs to do.<br />
        <strong>2. Walk ground together</strong> — including tracts that fit before they're widely marketed.<br />
        <strong>3. Offer with eyes open</strong> — honest pricing guidance and a fiduciary who works for you.<br />
        <strong>4. Close, and stay a neighbor</strong> — we're still here after the sale, ranching the same country you just bought into.
      </p>

      <p><a class="btn btn-green" href="/contact/">Start the conversation</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
